Z||000003||Raydar||04-26-2001||10:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>Its probably just the fuel pump relay but could be the fuel pump itself.  Either way, 500 bucks is a pretty darn good price so I would snatch it up.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't understand how it could be the fuel pump itself. If there is no power applied, it CAN'T keep running. I vote for the fuel pump relay or the oil pressure switch. The oil pressure switch is connected in parallel with the relay. (When you go to look at this, be careful. There are several oil pressure senders. One runs the pump. One runs the warning light. I think.) <P>Either way, $500 is a good price. Jump on it.<P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
